PS5 HDMI: EDID fallback when no connector is bound

PR #57 hands the bridge's EDID only to the one connector amdgpu binds; when
the routing looks ambiguous (more or fewer than one HDMI-like link in the
VBIOS), nothing is bound and no connector gets an EDID: the display shows
up as "generic", 1080p only. PR #57 was tested on fat consoles only, so
keep the pre-#57 behaviour as a fallback: with nothing bound, DisplayPort
connectors get the bridge's EDID as before (logged once).
---

--- a/drivers/ps5/hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/ps5/hdmi.c
@@ -1593,8 +1593,20 @@
 const struct drm_edid *ps5_hdmi_get_edid(struct drm_connector *connector)
 {
 	guard(mutex)(&hdmi_edid_lock);
-	if (hdmi_connector && connector == hdmi_connector && real_edid)
+	if (!real_edid)
+		return NULL;
+	if (hdmi_connector)
+		return connector == hdmi_connector ? drm_edid_dup(real_edid) : NULL;
+	/*
+	 * No connector bound (amdgpu found the routing ambiguous; PR #57 was only
+	 * tested on fat consoles): behave as before the binding, every DisplayPort
+	 * connector gets the bridge's EDID, instead of none at all ("generic
+	 * display", 1080p only).
+	 */
+	if (connector->connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_DisplayPort) {
+		pr_info_once("EDID not bound to a connector, using it for %s\n", connector->name);
 		return drm_edid_dup(real_edid);
+	}
 	return NULL;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(ps5_hdmi_get_edid);
